  "notes": "{嫌|きら}う is a godan verb meaning to hate or dislike, the verb form of the na-adjective ⟦{嫌|きら}い→嫌い：02871_kirai⟧.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- No standard intransitive pair\n- Pattern: [noun]⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{嫌|きら}う\n\n{嫌|きら}わない (neg), {嫌|きら}います (polite), {嫌|きら}って (te-form), {嫌|きら}った (past)\n\nKEY FORMS:\n- ⟦{嫌|きら}い→嫌い：02871_kirai⟧: dislike (na-adjective) - more common in speech\n- {嫌|きら}う: to dislike (verb) - sounds literary/formal\n- ⟦{嫌|きら}われる→嫌われる：24872_kirawareru⟧: to be disliked (passive) - very common\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{嫌|きら}われる: to be disliked by ~\n- 〜⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{嫌|きら}う: to dislike ~\n- ⟦{嫌|きら}われ{者|もの}→嫌われ者：noentry⟧: unpopular person\n\nINTENSITY SCALE:\n- ⟦{苦手|にがて}→苦手：03513_nigate⟧: not good with (mildest)\n- ⟦{嫌|きら}い→嫌い：02871_kirai⟧/⟦{嫌|きら}う→嫌う：02048_kirau⟧: dislike\n- ⟦{大嫌|だいきら}い→大嫌い：12178_daikirai⟧: hate\n- ⟦{憎|にく}む→憎む：00318_nikumu⟧: to hate (strongest)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{避|さ}ける→避ける：02109_sakeru⟧: to avoid\n- ⟦{嫌|いや}→嫌：10232_iya⟧: unpleasant, disagreeable\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {嫌|きら}って⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧: dislikes / hates (ongoing mental state)\n- ⟦{嫌|きら}われている→嫌われる：24872_kirawareru⟧: is disliked (passive resultative)\n- Note: {嫌|きら}う describes a standing emotional attitude, so the て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ form is used for \"someone dislikes ~,\" not \"is in the process of disliking.\" In everyday speech, the na-adjective ⟦{嫌|きら}い→嫌い：02871_kirai⟧ is far more common than the verb (⟦{野菜|やさい}→野菜：02265_yasai⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{嫌|きら}い→嫌い：02871_kirai⟧だ \"I don't like vegetables\"); {嫌|きら}って⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ tends to appear in writing or formal narration.",
